WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.765
The authors ran a preregistered, mixed-methods
study with thirty programmers,

00:00:04.845 --> 00:00:10.175
comparing three ways of presenting the same AI code
completions: no highlights at all,

00:00:10.255 --> 00:00:15.523
highlights based on generation probability, and
highlights based on a new edit model.

00:00:15.603 --> 00:00:20.431
The edit model is the key idea: instead of asking
how confident the model was,

00:00:20.511 --> 00:00:24.332
it predicts which tokens a human is actually likely
to change.

00:00:24.412 --> 00:00:26.345
This reframes the whole problem,

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:30.435
from surfacing model uncertainty to surfacing human
intervention,

00:00:30.515 --> 00:00:37.670
and the authors argue the same recipe could scale
up by learning from edit telemetry that products already collect.
